  "id": "rec-2025-05-20-crpt-119hrpt106-pt1-minority-views-17",
  "content": "<Rep. Jamie Raskin>: This bill also includes the Midnight Rules Relief Act. This measure would allow Republicans to bundle together lots of regulations--including all of the regulations adopted in the final 365 days of the prior administration--into a single package and then vote them down as a single jumbo resolution. This tactic would, of course, only be used to hide the most destructive deregulatory votes among dozens of others.\nThe presence of these and other provisions in this legislation suggests that this is not merely a budgetary bill, but one that includes significant, unrelated policy changes that may run afoul of the budget reconciliation process.\nIV. CONCLUSION\nFor all of the reasons discussed above, I urge my colleagues to oppose this legislation.\nJamie Raskin,\nRanking Member.\nCongressional Budget Office,\nU.S. Congress,",
